Z||000000||Songman||05-25-2001||05:53 PM||||Do you have any idea how to turn off that little graphic tool bar that pops up everytime you move your mouse over an image? I have an Indy Fiero picture as my backdrop so the stupid little bar stays up all the time!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||btoth||05-25-2001||06:23 PM||||How is IE6?  I downloaded it, but was kinda afraid to install it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||sjp777||05-25-2001||08:14 PM||||I don't think you can turn it off, but it should only pop up when your pointer is actually on the pic. If you're talking about having your indy pic set as an active desktop item, just right click anywhere on the desktop and check the option for "lock desktop items" from the popup menu. That way it truely becomes part of the background and your pointer won't effect it unless you unlock it.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_2.jpg">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||sjp777||05-25-2001||08:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by btoth:<BR><B>How is IE6?  I downloaded it, but was kinda afraid to install it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you have a fast PC, it's great. It might be pretty slow on an older PC. Try it and see, it's pretty easy to revert to the previous browser version if you don't like it, and no you won't have to re-download your old version||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||05-26-2001||02:25 AM||||IE6 is working great for me... I've got a fast PC with lots of memory. It really flies so far...<P>I don't like them having a bar that pops up over any graphic on my screen though.. that is where people start hating Microsoft.. especially when you can't turn the silly thing off...<P>Tried the right click/lock desktop thing.. Didn't work.. The bar still pops up whenever my mouse is anywhere on my background picture.... oh well, we'll figure something out in time... Thanks.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Songman||05-26-2001||03:42 AM||||Found it! I knew there had to be a way to get rid of this annoying little sucker!<P>To turn off the image toolbar<P>In Internet Explorer, on the Tools menu, click Internet Options. <BR>On the Advanced tab, under Multimedia, clear the Enable Image Toolbar check box. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||6
